 Changelog
 =========
 
+Unreleased
+----------
+- VerifiableRL can learn its policy from whole episodes: ``VerifiableRL(..., optimizer="group")``. For each training
+  sample the policy plays ``group_size`` episodes; an episode's advantage is its return minus the mean return of its
+  group, so whatever the group shares (the label, the slots nobody revealed) cancels and no value network is
+  needed; the policy is then improved on PPO's clipped objective (``clip_range``). This is GRPO (Shao et al., 2024)
+  without its division by the group's standard deviation, which makes a sample whose episodes differ only by a slot
+  cost weigh as much as one whose episodes differ by a right or a wrong call. Unlike the rollout targets, the return
+  includes the slot costs and the step penalty, so the policy learns *when to stop* from what continuing is worth.
+  It needs no rollouts: a pass over the samples costs a fraction of a rollout pass. ``optimizer="rollout"``, the
+  paper's method, stays the default, and nothing changes for existing code. New ``group_size``, ``group_batch``,
+  ``group_epochs``, ``group_lr`` and ``clip_range``; the supervisor then advises only when predicting. It is tuned
+  for short training: over many more updates than about a dozen it can get worse after reaching its best policy.
+
